WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.410
You told me in the commercial break

2
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.353
you wanted to,

3
00:00:02.353 --> 00:00:03.510
you brought something.

4
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.350
Yeah, I did.

5
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.183
I feel bad.

6
00:00:05.183 --> 00:00:06.016
I've never done your show before

7
00:00:06.016 --> 00:00:07.486
and you were so good to come and do

8
00:00:07.486 --> 00:00:10.879
the global initiative we do for university students

9
00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:12.829
and I feel like a schmuck.

10
00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:14.170
I've never done your show before.

11
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.489
(laughter)

12
00:00:15.489 --> 00:00:16.989
And you had to come to my neighborhood to do it.

13
00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:18.549
Yeah, I,

14
00:00:18.549 --> 00:00:19.965
now that you bring that all up,

15
00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:22.293
I'm kind of bitter about it all.

16
00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:23.922
(laughter)

17
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:24.762
I was fine,

18
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:26.041
I hadn't even really you know,

19
00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:26.913
and then you bring it up

20
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:27.898
and now I'm angry.

21
00:00:27.898 --> 00:00:28.771
Here's what I did.

22
00:00:28.771 --> 00:00:29.648
I know you like bobble heads

23
00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:32.167
so I'll be a guest all the time now.

24
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.146
Oh look at that.

25
00:00:33.146 --> 00:00:35.396
(applause)

26
00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:40.069
The great thing,

27
00:00:40.069 --> 00:00:41.921
(laughter)

28
00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:43.639
the great thing about my bobble head is

29
00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:45.394
you can turn it into a bad political joke

30
00:00:45.394 --> 00:00:46.932
that every time you say something

31
00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:48.769
you can just tump me on the head

32
00:00:48.769 --> 00:00:50.065
and I'll agree with you every time.

33
00:00:50.065 --> 00:00:52.566
(laughter)

34
00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:54.209
Yep.

35
00:00:54.209 --> 00:00:55.119
Yep.

36
00:00:55.119 --> 00:00:56.453
I got to put you

37
00:00:56.453 --> 00:00:57.611
right there next to Eisenhower,

38
00:00:57.611 --> 00:00:58.488
how's that?

39
00:00:58.488 --> 00:00:59.725
Is that alright with you?

40
00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:00.672
It's a good thing.

41
00:01:00.672 --> 00:01:01.545
Yeah, different parties,

42
00:01:01.545 --> 00:01:02.511
but both I think, you know--

43
00:01:02.511 --> 00:01:04.761
(applause)

44
00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:07.000
It's funny, you know,

45
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.431
it was a different world,

46
00:01:09.431 --> 00:01:11.003
but a couple years ago,

47
00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.351
in this scholar's rating of presidential

48
00:01:13.351 --> 00:01:14.351
performance,

49
00:01:15.344 --> 00:01:17.638
Eisenhower and I were back to back.

50
00:01:17.638 --> 00:01:18.625
But I always

51
00:01:18.625 --> 00:01:19.829
liked him

52
00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:20.662
because

53
00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:23.590
he ordered the integration

54
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.275
of Little Rock Central High School.

55
00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:26.675
Yeah, yeah.

56
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:27.781
He federalized the national guard.

57
00:01:27.781 --> 00:01:28.859
(applause)

58
00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:29.806
Yeah.

59
00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:30.646
And--

60
00:01:30.646 --> 00:01:31.621
Very impressive figure.

61
00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:33.510
It was a big deal in my childhood, you know,

62
00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.596
that he,

63
00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:35.471
he did that.

64
00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:36.451
He had to call out,

65
00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:39.200
he had to send in the 101st Airborne Division,

66
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.130
but he first nationalized the

67
00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.052
National Guard to stop the governor

68
00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:45.383
who had blocked nine black children.

69
00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:47.689
We just celebrated the 60th anniversary of that.

70
00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:49.673
Eight of them are still alive.

71
00:01:49.673 --> 00:01:51.147
(applause)

72
00:01:51.147 --> 00:01:52.598
They've had remarkable lives.

73
00:01:52.598 --> 00:01:54.487
(applause)

74
00:01:54.487 --> 00:01:56.077
And,

75
00:01:56.077 --> 00:01:57.415
it shaped my whole life.

76
00:01:57.415 --> 00:01:59.948
So, when the chips were down,

77
00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:01.609
he decided he believed in the constitution.

78
00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:02.608
Yeah, yeah.

79
00:02:02.608 --> 00:02:05.441
God bless him.
It's a good deal.

